  "id": "Compound::DB00387 - Gene::1131",
  "verbalization": "Procyclidine exhibits a strong binding interaction with Chrm4, as evidenced by multiple paths with high confidence scores (0.6953, 0.6815, and 0.6811). This binding is linked to the participation of Chrm4 in various receptor activities, including G-protein coupled acetylcholine receptor activity, muscarinic acetylcholine receptor activity, and G-protein coupled neurotransmitter receptor activity. These activities are all mediated through Chrm3, suggesting a mechanistic pathway where Procyclidine influences Chrm4, which in turn modulates Chrm3 through receptor-mediated signaling. The integrated evidence implies that Procyclidine may act on Chrm4 to regulate Chrm3 through a G-protein-coupled pathway, potentially affecting downstream signaling processes. The consistent involvement of Chrm4 in multiple receptor activities and its direct participation in Chrm3 highlights a plausible mechanism by which Procyclidine could influence Chrm3, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
